### Testing

The plan is exercised with a tabletop at least once a year, in line with the annual cadence the clinic chose, and sooner after any significant change. The **Incident Commander** (IT Manager) facilitates. The Executive Sponsor, Technical Lead, Communications Lead and Legal and Compliance Lead must attend; Northwind IT is invited.

Each exercise produces a dated after-action report that records who attended, the scenario, the decisions made, strengths, gaps, and action items with an owner and a due date. The report is kept with the plan and is the evidence presented to the SOC 2 auditor and to Coalition at renewal.

### Review triggers

The plan is reviewed, and re-approved if changed, after any of:

- a real incident of any severity;
- a major change to systems, hosting or the identity provider, such as moving off Athena or changing the patient portal;
- an audit finding or a change in compliance obligations;
- a tabletop exercise;
- and in any case at least 60 days before the next audit or renewal on 2027-03-15.

### Approval

The CEO approves each version by name and date. The IT Manager records the version, the date, and what changed in the version history. The previous version is kept for the record and is never edited.
